+    // PokeDaisy: fast-forward's frame skip. Before each frame the host says whether it and the next one will be seen
+    // (SkipDraw / SkipDrawNext). A frame runs lines 0-262: its 2D lines 0-191 draw what's on screen now, its line 215
+    // starts the next frame's 3D and line 262 the next frame's first sprites - so those follow SkipDrawNext, decided at
+    // 215 (SkippingFrame, which the 3D renderer reads and which holds through the next frame), and a frame's 2D lines
+    // are left out only when its 3D was too (the threaded renderer's line count stays in step). Engine A's display
+    // capture on (the game reads the picture back) draws whatever. Not hardware state: never saved, and nothing the
+    // game reads depends on it (BG reference points and mosaic restart at every VBlank).
+public:
